@startuml
' What: the two clocks (D-39): ordinary turns for the body, generations for the soul.
' Shows: pressure piles up turn by turn; a generation starts after about 5 turns or when the pressure crosses a threshold;
'        at the generation change the body is read, the Choice of Fate runs, and the pressure is reset.
' Source: brainstorming-base.md, D-25, D-39, D-48. Open: the exact pressure threshold.
title Two clocks: turns and generations (D-39)
start
repeat
  :Turn: produce, build, research, move, fight;
  :World events and neighbours add pressure p to the lines;
  :The profile adds pressure toward each line's current pole;
repeat while (generation due?\n(about 5 turns, or pressure over threshold)) is (no) not (yes)
:Generation: read the body, Choice of Fate, profile update;
:New climate and era policy act until the next generation;
:Pressure p is reset;
stop
@enduml
